  "findings": {
    "identityAndReuse": "Fiscal Economics BSc, primarily Dutch with shared English courses, full-time, no formal specialisations under B6 Art1.1. Fresh programme response SHA e89895cd574a6ae176ce7b2faa8b1f0af034a33311be8b8e87d772bb6fd10979 and OER SHA6c2506ff8c263cfe295ec66b025eaa99bae217e5680ecbee7c39d6dc268be7c4 exactly match prior current-audit bodies. Preserve membership/credits and unaffected external research. Current R&R SHA88f5e313daf4ae37d2dbc47403ff8f3df77c053328f0053c82ac5944b20a8a83 also unchanged.",
    "hierarchyAndConflict": "Read actual adopted EB B6 Art3.4: EU Tax3313GEBRVY requires6012B0225+6012B0226, both earlier in this degree. PartA1.1 applies A+B to all regular programme students; PartA4.1.4 identifies B and catalogue requirements. The faculty rule establishes academic progression but does not explicitly discharge the shared course separate administrative minor condition. Current56800 still names that minor. Do not treat the Law case as determinative, but do not invent a faculty precedence/eligibility exception from academic prerequisite satisfaction.",
    "officialAlternative": "Public programme-selected OER index still links same OER and current R&R, with no applicable2026–2027 erratum. Current EB-specific registration requires catalogue eligibility or an individual waiver application before registration closes. Timely compulsory-course place guarantee and GLASS capacity priority do not show an awarded cohort waiver. No account, login, registration/waiver submission or university contact used.",
    "restrictedChoiceCorrection": "Dated year3 group is exactly6EC from six listed options. The old canonical left a generic restricted slot. Read actual60706 BusinessAnalytics: EB bachelor enrolment except BusinessAnalytics; mandatory basic statistical knowledge such as regression. Actual57335 QDA1 lists probabilities/inference/correlation, no express regression training;60863 is fiscal ethics/philosophy, not regression. This does not prove students cannot know regression, but invalidates prior assertion that QDA1 establishes it. Select next-listed57465/6013B0564Y CorporateSocialResponsibility, whose explicit EB bachelor-entry condition this path meets. It is an actual restricted option, not invented open space, and substantively fits business responsibility/ethical questions. Selection is based on external curriculum/order/confirmed requirements, not ease of UCR matching.",
    "externalContentAndProgression": "Read current required-course content for28 additional entries, selected CSR, BA, EUtax, seminar/thesis. B6 accepts Dutch FA1 for advanced accounting despite shared English links. FA3 recommends FA2 but B6 hard requirement is FA1. Finance1 precedes Finance2. Earlier general/business tax supports advanced corporate/VAT/international/DGA/profit sequence. Payroll3EC and TaxTechnology3EC retained; research-foundations course is ethics/philosophy, not an empirical-regression module.",
    "research": "Actual seminar requires entire firsttwo years and120EC, develops proposal/introduction/firstliteraturechapter. Advanced tax courses, including EUtax, are recommended preparation, not additional hard seminar prerequisites. Thesis6EC requires seminar, independent analysis/literature, progress reports; final discussion is discretionary. Do not transplant TaxLaw mandatory oral-defence rule or120EC/threeweek deadline into this programme.",
    "credits": "Full membership32 positive-credit components once one6EC option selected,180EC. Partial31components177EC, excluded only EUtax3EC. Generic minor/elective pages do not turn the6EC restricted slot into a30EC minor or additional free space."
